<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The problems below consist of pairs of equivalent expressions: one in standard form and the other in factored form. Note that the leading coefficients on the quadratic terms are all 1.</para>
<para>Find the missing numbers.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise><exercise>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-input-ack">
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>18 and 17, respectively. The completed expression is \(x^2+18x +17\).</para>
  </div>
<problem>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2 \;+\) __\(x\;+\) __ and \((x + 1)(x + 17)\)</item>
    </list>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Enter the missing numbers.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
</exercise><!--Interaction End -->
<br/>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise><exercise>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-input-ack">
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 7. The completed expression is \((x + 2)(x + 7)\).</para>
  </div>
<problem>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2+9x +14\) and \((x + 2)(x\; +\) __\()\)</item>
    </list>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Enter the missing number.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
</exercise><!--Interaction End -->
<br/>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise><exercise>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-input-ack">
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 5. The completed expression is \((x − 2)(x − 5)\).</para>
  </div>
<problem>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2−7x +10\) and \((x − 2)(x\; −\) __\()\)</item>
    </list>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Enter the missing number.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
</exercise><!--Interaction End -->
<br/>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise><exercise>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-input-ack">
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 4 and 5. The completed expression is \((x − 4)(x − 5)\).</para>
  </div>
<problem>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2−9x +20\) and \((x\; −\) __)\((x\; −\) __\()\)</item>
